BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Author event with mother and son duo Jyoti and Auyon Mukharji at M
 orgenstern Books
DTSTART;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20260921T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20260921T190000
UID:b663add511adcc69f0acb153e74c8474@ipm.org
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims4/default/b03b
 62d/2147483647/strip/true/crop/480x480+0+0/resize/254x254!/quality/90/?url
 =http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F5d%2Fe9%2F147865e046ea937e
 781a2607a903%2Fjyoti-and-auyon-mukharji-sep-21-2026-website.png
DESCRIPTION:Join us for an evening with mother and son duo Jyoti and Auyon
  Mukharji\, who will be sharing from their cookbook\, Heartland Masala: An
  Indian Cookbook from an American Kitchen. \nABOUT THE BOOK:\nHeartland Ma
 sala pairs 99 recipes from Indian cooking instructor Jyoti Mukharji with c
 ultural and historical essays by her son Auyon Mukharji. An effervescent c
 elebration of Indian cuisine and the American immigrant experience\, this 
 beautiful cookbook is playful\, informative\, and utterly original.\n 2025
  Foreword INDIES Book of the Year Awards Gold Winner in Cooking\nReal Simp
 le\, Food Editor's Top Cookbook Pick\nSlate\, Top 10 Best Recipes of the Y
 ear\nThe Boston Globe\, Best Cookbooks for Holiday Giving\nKansas City Mag
 azine\, Top Gifts to Give and Receive\n Filled with rich storytelling\, st
 unning visuals\, and a blend of modern and traditional dishes\, this book 
 is both a heartfelt portrait of one Midwestern family and a practical guid
 e to cooking incredible Indian meals at home.\n Here's what makes Heartlan
 d Masala special:\n• Delicious\, Accessible Recipes — 99 carefully tes
 ted dishes bring Indian flavors into your kitchen\, with ingredients and m
 ethods tailored for American home cooks.\n• Cultural Essays & Family Sto
 ries — Fresh\, insightful\, and often humorous essays explore the immigr
 ant cooking philosophy\, the Mukharjis' mother-son dynamic\, and the many 
 quirks of Indian culinary history.\n• Illustrations & Stunning Photograp
 hy — A 32-page full-color photo insert plus original art make this a gor
 geous centerpiece for your kitchen or coffee table.\n• Step-by-Step Guid
 ance — Jyoti and Auyon include illustrations that demystify complex tech
 niques\, along with spice shopping tips to build confidence and skill.\n A
  feast for culturally curious readers and adventurous cooks alike\, Heartl
 and Masala is unlike any Indian cookbook you've seen before.\nABOUT THE AU
 THORS:\nJyoti Mukharji is a chef\, teacher\, and retired physician. She im
 migrated to the US from India in the late 1970s\, and she began teaching w
 eekly Indian cooking classes out of her home in Prairie Village\, KS in 20
 10. Jyoti has since welcomed several thousand students into her kitchen\, 
 and her writing and teaching have been celebrated in press and radio outle
 ts across the Midwest. Jyoti's team includes her husband Jhulan (art direc
 tor)\, her eldest son Arnob (grocery shopping deputy)\, her middle son Auy
 on (musical guest)\, and her youngest son Aroop (copy editor).\n Auyon Muk
 harji is a musician\, writer\, and culinary historian who spends most of h
 is time thinking about food. He studied biology at Williams College and wa
 s awarded a Watson Fellowship in 2007 to study self-expression in folk mus
 ic. Since 2009\, Auyon has toured with\, and cooked for\, the acclaimed in
 die-folk band Darlingside. He otherwise finds time to work in and around k
 itchens (and farms) in both his hometown of Kansas City and his adopted st
 ate-of-residence of Massachusetts.\nTickets: https://www.eventbrite.com/e/
 jyoti-auyon-mukharji-on-heartland-masala-tickets-1991993954541
LOCATION:Morgenstern Books\, 849 S Auto Mall Rd\, Bloomington\, Indiana 47
 401
URL:https://www.ipm.org/community-calendar/event/author-event-with-mother-
 and-son-duo-jyoti-and-auyon-mukharji-at-morgenstern-books-24-08-2026-10-17
 -26
X-SOURCE:WFIU Community Calendar
X-SOURCE-URL:https://www.ipm.org/community-calendar/
END:VEVENT
