SUMMARY:“DIGITAL TRANSFORMATION AND JAPAN’S POLITICAL ECONOMY”
DTSTART;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20260922T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20260922T171000
UID:1988e356d9f982b16c0a959dede4f983@ipm.org
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims4/default/ca44
 c45/2147483647/strip/true/crop/840x1080+0+0/resize/254x327!/quality/90/?ur
 l=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Ff7%2F5d%2Fb7e41d00430596e
 9925d5f9611fb%2F20260922-21jpsi-shimizu-flyer.png
DESCRIPTION:Presented by 21JPSI\nIn this public lecture\, Prof. Shimizu wi
 ll discuss lessons for businesses and governments from Japan’s experienc
 e with “digital transformation.” Japan’s traditional sectors are bei
 ng replaced by digital systems that paradoxically demand fewer people but 
 also create new jobs. Meanwhile\, emerging technologies are opening fresh 
 opportunities for Japanese companies to compete globally. Prof. Shimizu’
 s prepared remarks will be followed by audience Q&A and discussion.\n This
  21JPSI event is open to all students\, faculty\, staff\, and the general 
 public. It is made possible thanks to a generous grant from the Japan Foun
 dation. Please join us!
LOCATION:Global and International Studies Building\, 355 Eagleson Ave\, Bl
 oomington\, Indiana 47405
