ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims4/default/bb1b
 f68/2147483647/strip/true/crop/1920x1080+0+0/resize/254x143!/quality/90/?u
 rl=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Ffb%2Fe4%2F2b203a5a4f9e8b
 4cd2e9173c8107%2Ftimeless-16x9.jpg
DESCRIPTION:Presented by WFIU/WTIU\nJoin fellow WTIU viewers and station s
 taff for a special screening in Mitchell\, IN of Timeless: Don Fischer’s
  Half-Century Broadcasting IU Sports on September 22nd . \n Timeless tells
  the story of the legendary broadcaster whose career spans generations of 
 IU fans and athletes. Through archival footage\, historic radio calls\, in
 terviews\, and personal reflections\, the documentary explores Fischer’s
  unlikely rise from a small-town Illinois upbringing to becoming one of th
 e most recognizable voices in college sports.\n Following the screening of
  Timeless \, stick around for a screening of A Team That Wouldn't Be Beat 
 \, a rarely-seen documentary chronicling the 1975-76 Indiana Hoosiers men'
 s basketball team and their undefeated national championship season\, rece
 ntly resurfaced from the IU Archives.
LOCATION:Thompson Recital Hall of Depauw University\, 605 S College Ave\, 
 Greencastle\, Indiana 46135
