BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Fall Ballet – Choreography by Christian Claessens\, George Balan
 chine\, Caili Quan\, and James Whiteside
DTSTART;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20261003T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20261003T235900
UID:d976318df16240cf609637237b527a33@ipm.org
DESCRIPTION:White Shadows\nChristian Claessens\n Longtime Jacobs faculty m
 ember Christian Claessens teams up with the Jacobs Percussion Department t
 o create this world premiere based on the last three movements of Steve Re
 ich’s Sextet\, employing marimbas\, vibraphones\, bass drums\, and more.
  The eight dancers embody movement from pulsations to melodic patterns to 
 rhythmic ambiguity.\n Christian Claessens\, Choreographer\n Joseph Gramley
 \, Conductor and Chamber Music Coach\n Blake Kile\, Lighting Designer\n Va
 lse-Fantaisie\nGeorge Balanchine\n Attended by their single partner\, five
  ballerinas move in a whirl of perpetual motion to Mikhail Glinka’s walt
 zing rhythms. Although it was popularly called “the Melancholy Waltz\,
 ” this 1967 rendering is fast and light and was originally presented as 
 the second section of Glinkiana\, which featured former IU Distinguished P
 rofessor Violette Verdy in its New York City Ballet premiere.\n George Bal
 anchine\, Choreographer\n Kyra Nichols\, Stager\n Blake Kile\, Lighting De
 signer\n Dignity in Restraint\nCaili Quan\n Born to a Chamorro Filipino fa
 mily in Guam\, Caili Quan created this punchy work on New York City Ballet
  dancers to Beethoven’s String Quartet No. 12. Her love for “showing p
 eople the music” is on full display as she corresponds five major chords
  to the five core emotions of anger\, fear\, disgust\, joy\, and sadness.\
 n Caili Quan\, Choreographer\n Andrea Yorita\, Stager\n Blake Kile\, Light
 ing Designer\n World Premiere\nJames Whiteside\n A principal dancer and ch
 oreographer with American Ballet Theatre\, James Whiteside is also a pop m
 usic performer\, model\, drag queen\, podcast host\, and author. He brings
  his wildly eclectic style to Jacobs for several weeks as he creates his l
 atest work\, with the students of the Ballet Department.\n James Whiteside
 \, Choreographer\n Michael Breeden\, Stager\n Blake Kile\, Lighting Design
 er\nTickets: https://am.ticketmaster.com/iumac/buy
LOCATION:Musical Arts Center\, 201 S. Eagleson Ave\, Bloomington\, Indiana
  47405
URL:https://www.ipm.org/community-calendar/event/fall-ballet-choreography-
 by-christian-claessens-george-balanchine-caili-quan-and-james-whiteside-01
 -09-2026-11-21-05
X-SOURCE:WFIU Community Calendar
X-SOURCE-URL:https://www.ipm.org/community-calendar/
END:VEVENT
