BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Sarah Jarosz: 10 Years of Undercurrent
DTSTART;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20261003T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20261003T223000
UID:9f5266410b9c081850de12f437eaa4f7@ipm.org
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims4/default/ee6e
 ba7/2147483647/strip/true/crop/640x640+0+0/resize/254x254!/quality/90/?url
 =http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F38%2F4e%2F8f99c54a4612bc9a
 ae9fb57784fa%2Fopen-uri20260302-658-gjecnv.jpeg
DESCRIPTION:Presented by Buskirk-Chumley Theater\nOriginally from Wimberle
 y\, Texas\, Sarah Jarosz is a six-time GRAMMY Award-winning singer\, songw
 riter\, and multi-instrumentalist. Since her recorded debut in 2009\, she 
 has released seven solo albums and two albums with I’m With Her\, her ba
 nd with Sara Watkins and Aoife O’Donovan.\n In addition to her multiple 
 GRAMMY\, Americana Music Association\, and Folk Alliance awards\, her work
  has received widespread critical praise from publications including Rolli
 ng Stone\, The New York Times\, and USA Today. Jarosz has appeared three t
 imes on PBS’s legendary Austin City Limits television show and numerous 
 times on A Prairie Home Companion\, Live From Here\, and the Grand Ole Opr
 y. She is currently based in Nashville\, Tennessee.\n Jordan Tice is an aw
 ard-winning guitarist and songwriter described by the Fretboard Journal as
  “quite simply\, one of our favorite acoustic guitarists performing toda
 y.” He has 7 projects to his name as a solo artist and 6 as a founding m
 ember of the string band\, Hawktail.\n Equally virtuosic as a flatpicker a
 nd fingerstylist\, and with a casual vocal style\, Tice conjures ingredien
 ts from far-flung worlds with ease. His performances call upon the reperto
 ries of American and British Isles folk\, bluegrass\, blues\, and pop-orie
 nted songs\, and though his earlier releases are instrumental in focus\, h
 e has been carefully honing his craft as a singer-songwriter in his most r
 ecent work. This includes his albums Motivational Speakeasy (produced by K
 enneth Pattengale of The Milk Carton Kids and praised by NPR Music as “a
  really wonderful record”)\, Wild Rose of Morning (a collaboration with 
 Andrew Marlin and Christian Sedelmyer)\, and Badlettsville.\n He has perfo
 rmed at festivals such as the Grey Fox Bluegrass Festival\, Green Mountain
  Bluegrass and Roots\, Red Wing Roots\, Wintergrass Music Festival\, and t
 he Strawberry Music Festival and opened for artists like Watchhouse\, I’
 m With Her\, The Milk Carton Kids\, and Madison Cunningham. In addition to
  his solo and collaborative work\, he has performed and recorded as a side
 man with Americana artists such as David Rawlings\, Yola\, Andrew Marlin\,
  and Aoife O’Donovan.\nTickets: https://buskirkchumley.org/events/sarah-
 jarosz-10-years-of-undercurrent-december-3-2026/
LOCATION:Buskirk-Chumley Theater\, 114 E Kirkwood Ave\, Bloomington\, Indi
 ana 47408
URL:https://www.ipm.org/community-calendar/event/sarah-jarosz-10-years-of-
 undercurrent-28-08-2026-12-43-58
X-SOURCE:WFIU Community Calendar
X-SOURCE-URL:https://www.ipm.org/community-calendar/
END:VEVENT
