BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Baroque Orchestra – Ingrid Matthews\, director
DTSTART;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20261004T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20261004T180000
UID:0ac5344b71f55022185b2a8906f6666d@ipm.org
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims4/default/549b
 3da/2147483647/strip/true/crop/240x180+0+0/resize/254x191!/quality/90/?url
 =http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fcb%2F54%2Fdcb71ddb4da58806
 b3c37ff1e5b2%2F8388-matthews-ingrid-2021fa-webcal-js-rev-1628179143.jpg
DESCRIPTION:Repertoire to be announced\n About the Director\n Ingrid Matth
 ews is professor of practice in historical performance (baroque violin) at
  the Indiana University Jacobs School of Music. A graduate of IU\, where s
 he studied with Josef Gingold and Stanley Ritchie\, Matthews is one of tod
 ay’s most respected baroque violinists. Since winning first prize in the
  Erwin Bodky International Competition for Early Music in 1989\, she has a
 ppeared as soloist\, guest director\, chamber musician\, and concertmaster
  with leading early music ensembles\, including the New York Collegium\, A
 ustralian Brandenburg Orchestra\, Boston Early Music Festival Orchestra\, 
 Ars Lyrica (Houston)\, Tafelmusik Baroque Orchestra (Toronto)\, Musica Pac
 ifica (San Francisco)\, and many others. Matthews cofounded the Seattle Ba
 roque Orchestra in 1994 and served as its music director until 2013. Matth
 ews has won high critical acclaim for her extensive discography. Her recor
 ding J. S. Bach: Complete Sonatas and Partitas for Violin was named “top
  recommendation for this music … on either period or modern instruments
 ” by American Record Guide. She also plays jazz and swing styles and is 
 active as a visual artist.
LOCATION:Auer Hall\, Simon Music Center\, 200 S. Eagleson Ave\, Bloomingto
 n\, Indiana 47405
URL:https://www.ipm.org/community-calendar/event/baroque-orchestra-ingrid-
 matthews-director-01-09-2026-11-27-59
X-SOURCE:WFIU Community Calendar
X-SOURCE-URL:https://www.ipm.org/community-calendar/
END:VEVENT
